From: Mili <noreply@mili.local>
Date: Wed, 22 Jan 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mili: Add legacy NMS class name remapping


Some plugins still reference pre-1.20.5 spigot NMS class names that have
since been renamed in upstream Mojang (and therefore also in spigot) and
which the Paper reflection-rewriter therefore cannot resolve, because
io.papermc.paper.util.ObfHelper only knows about current
spigot (obfuscated) <-> mojang (public) name pairs.

This shim consults a small curated table maintained in
fun.bm.mili.nms.LegacyNMSMappings before falling back to the original
ObfHelper lookup, so that reflective Class.forName(...) calls made by
plugins such as CustomCrops 3.6.x for
net.minecraft.server.ScoreboardServer (now ServerScoreboard) succeed
instead of throwing NoClassDefFoundError.

Plugins that hard-code an NMS class symbol in their bytecode (e.g. an
NMS-version-specific implementation class that extends a renamed class)
still cannot be fixed at this layer and must be updated by their authors.


diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/pluginremap/reflect/PaperReflection.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/pluginremap/reflect/PaperReflection.java
index 92bc8e4933ff13764fa2ac7f3729216332e202c9..0c1bff165c0b41464728c869988dc321bd5e95d5 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/pluginremap/reflect/PaperReflection.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/pluginremap/reflect/PaperReflection.java
@@ -51,6 +51,12 @@
 
     @Override
     protected String mapClassName(final String name) {
+        // Mili start - legacy NMS remapping shim
+        final String legacyMapped = fun.bm.mili.nms.LegacyNMSMappings.mapClassName(name);
+        if (legacyMapped != name) {
+            return legacyMapped;
+        }
+        // Mili end - legacy NMS remapping shim
         final ObfHelper.@Nullable ClassMapping mapping = this.mappingsByObfName.get(name);
         return mapping != null ? mapping.mojangName() : removeCraftBukkitRelocation(name);
     }
